From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 15:12:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] complete Folia's synchronization of PaperPermissionManager

Folia wrapped every method of that class in synchronized (this) except two:
getDefaultPermissions(boolean), which copies defaultPerms().get(op), and
removePermission(String), which mutates permissions().

The reader is the one that bites. ImmutableSet.copyOf sizes an array from the
set and then fills it, so a concurrent add from another thread's addPermission
aborts the copy with ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException out of
LinkedHashMap.keysToArray. Two threads really do register permissions during
boot: Luminol loads its config on a ForkJoinPool thread and registers Leaves
command permissions from there while the main thread does the same. Measured on
the 38-jar mirror: 3 aborted starts in about 12.

Only a set copy runs under the monitor - no plugin code, no callback, no second
lock - so no lock-ordering edge is added, and the writers keep calling
dirtyPermissibles outside their own block exactly as before.

removePermission is fixed alongside it with no crash of its own on record: a
class synchronized everywhere except one writer is not synchronized.

diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPermissionManager.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPermissionManager.java
index 9ddbb2d72e11c6abbbdb866f3010f276efceda41..4ebf520126ad9a9e96ce394e91660751c2fbc8d3 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPermissionManager.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPermissionManager.java
@@ -77,7 +77,21 @@ abstract class PaperPermissionManager implements PermissionManager {
     @Override
     @NotNull
     public Set<Permission> getDefaultPermissions(boolean op) {
+        // Lecithin start - Folia synchronized the writers of defaultPerms() but not this reader.
+        // ImmutableSet.copyOf sizes the array first and then fills it, so a concurrent add from
+        // another thread's addPermission/recalculatePermissionDefaults aborts the copy with
+        // ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException. That is not hypothetical: Luminol loads its config on a
+        // ForkJoin thread and registers Leaves command permissions from there while the main thread
+        // is still registering its own, and the server dies during boot roughly one start in four.
+        // Nothing but a set copy runs under the monitor, so this adds no lock-ordering edge - which
+        // is why the writers deliberately call dirtyPermissibles outside their own block.
+        if (!fun.bm.lecithin.config.modules.CompatConfig.permissionLocking) {
+            return ImmutableSet.copyOf(this.defaultPerms().get(op)); // stock body, kill switch
+        }
+        synchronized (this) {
         return ImmutableSet.copyOf(this.defaultPerms().get(op));
+        }
+        // Lecithin end
     }
 
 
@@ -89,7 +103,18 @@ abstract class PaperPermissionManager implements PermissionManager {
 
     @Override
     public void removePermission(@NotNull String name) {
+        // Lecithin start - the second method Folia's synchronization sweep missed. Every other
+        // mutation of permissions() holds the monitor; this one races getPermissions()'s copy the
+        // same way getDefaultPermissions raced above. No crash observed from it yet - it is fixed
+        // because a class that is synchronized everywhere except one writer is not synchronized.
+        if (!fun.bm.lecithin.config.modules.CompatConfig.permissionLocking) {
+            this.permissions().remove(name.toLowerCase(java.util.Locale.ENGLISH)); // stock body, kill switch
+            return;
+        }
+        synchronized (this) {
         this.permissions().remove(name.toLowerCase(java.util.Locale.ENGLISH));
+        }
+        // Lecithin end
     }
 
     @Override
